 class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>","key":"yPGdSsQz6h"},{"type":"text","value":" or ","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"OnWVFqZ4ET"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"x = 1","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x = 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>","key":"GR6KMwFJBi"},{"type":"text","value":". There, the polynomial must extrapolate beyond its eight training points, and polynomials of high degree swing far away from the data. Repeated on 2,000 training sets drawn in the same way, each with a new random assignment of points to folds, cross-validation chooses degree 3 in 86% of the cases and degree 5 in 11%. Comparing the five degrees costs 25 trainings.","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"QbMXYbRWto"}],"key":"uPvEahexc8"}],"key":"L60xtTdRX1"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Training Pipeline","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"ToHE0fuiEh"}],"identifier":"the-training-pipeline","label":"The Training Pipeline","html_id":"the-training-pipeline","implicit":true,"key":"mbUGWWvc7b"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"crossReference","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"vnd694czkN"},{"type":"text","value":"2","key":"OAIEcc6ejv"}],"identifier":"fig-model-development-pipeline","label":"fig-model-development-pipeline","kind":"figure","template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"2","resolved":true,"html_id":"fig-model-development-pipeline","key":"XjsvbLvGUb"},{"type":"text","value":" puts the steps together. First, we split the data into a training set and a test set, keeping about 20% for the final assessment and neither using nor looking at it during training (step 1). Second, we split the training data into a training set and a validation set, again with about 20% for validation, or we use k-fold cross-validation when data is limited (step 2). Third, we train the model on the training set only (step 3). Training iterates over ","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"hDPLOuF2Mj"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"epochs","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"MBw8CYlGJK"}],"key":"iloSlP6Fs3"},{"type":"text","value":", where one epoch is one pass over all training examples, until the performance converges or it becomes clear that the current hyperparameters are poor.","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"HOqmYhy7Vq"}],"key":"hOdCHk8oLW"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/mmir-unibasel-hs26/book/build/figure_A_7-6eaead6c91e9b0a9ef6da76dd1363d80.png","alt":"The model development pipeline in five steps, from splitting the data to the final assessment on the test set.","width":"95%","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"Qo9B6ksboL","urlSource":"images/figure_A_7.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"fig-model-development-pipeline","identifier":"fig-model-development-pipeline","html_id":"fig-model-development-pipeline","enumerator":"2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"JIQlBQpOC4"},{"type":"text","value":"2","key":"NfByFSQftZ"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"mtddKHrCxs"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"pMTL9Lng2E"},{"type":"text","value":"The model development pipeline in five steps, from splitting the data to the final assessment on the test set.","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"aQPHOGNKlW"}],"key":"xZmykxwReQ"}],"key":"KaI7BxE2CB"}],"label":"fig-model-development-pipeline","identifier":"fig-model-development-pipeline","enumerator":"2","html_id":"fig-model-development-pipeline","key":"r3TWfcf2YY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fourth, we validate the model, adjust the hyperparameters, and repeat steps 2 to 4. With the best hyperparameters, we retrain the model, with more epochs if needed (step 4). Finally, we assess the model on the test set and compare it with other methods (step 5). If we iterate the whole process, each new round needs fresh test data, because the previous test set has influenced our decisions. In competitions, the contestants receive only the final assessment and cannot inspect where and why their model failed.","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"MToDIbwj4V"}],"key":"gWe3ZVMLGa"}],"key":"kRtYAwXpTg"}],"key":"C6LcSayuvV"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Over- and Underfitting","url":"/over-and-underfitting","group":"Appendix (Optional Reading)"},"next":{"title":"Summary","url":"/summary-9","group":"Appendix (Optional Reading)"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}